  "flashcards": [
    {
      "id": "mq-fc01",
      "front": "Quotient rule",
      "back": "x<sup>a</sup> / x<sup>b</sup> = x<sup>a−b</sup> (x ≠ 0). Same base, dividing → <b>subtract</b> the exponents (top minus bottom).",
      "figure": {
        "alt": "Five x tiles over two x tiles. Two pairs are crossed out, leaving three x tiles on top.",
        "chips": { "num": { "n": 5, "text": "x" }, "den": { "n": 2, "text": "x" }, "cancel": 2, "rhs": "x³", "ask": false }
      },
      "figureSide": "back"
    },
    {
      "id": "mq-fc02",
      "front": "When the exponents match",
      "back": "x<sup>a</sup> / x<sup>a</sup> = x<sup>0</sup> = 1. Example: 9³ / 9³ = 1."
    },
    {
      "id": "mq-fc03",
      "front": "When the bottom is bigger",
      "back": "You get a negative exponent: x³ / x⁷ = x⁻⁴ = 1/x⁴. Final answers usually use only positive exponents."
    },
    {
      "id": "mq-fc04",
      "front": "Negative exponent",
      "back": "x<sup>−a</sup> = 1/x<sup>a</sup>. It means \"one over\", not a negative number: 2⁻³ = 1/8."
    },
    {
      "id": "mq-fc05",
      "front": "Coefficients",
      "back": "Divide the numbers in front like normal: 18x⁶ / 6x² = 3x⁴. Keep the sign: −15 ÷ 5 = −3."
    },
    {
      "id": "mq-fc06",
      "front": "More than one variable",
      "back": "Do each variable separately: a with a, b with b. 12x⁷y³ / 4x²y⁵ = 3x⁵/y²."
    },
    {
      "id": "mq-fc07",
      "front": "Power of a quotient",
      "back": "(x/y)<sup>a</sup> = x<sup>a</sup>/y<sup>a</sup>. The power goes on top and bottom: (x³/y²)⁴ = x¹²/y⁸."
    },
    {
      "id": "mq-fc08",
      "front": "Two common mistakes",
      "back": "Don't subtract the coefficients (8x⁶/2x³ is 4x³, not 6x³). Don't divide the exponents (x⁶/x³ is x³, not x²)."
    },
    {
      "id": "mq-fc09",
      "front": "\"Quotient rule\": which one?",
      "back": "In calculus, \"quotient rule\" means a rule for derivatives of fractions (f/g)′. That's a different topic. On this quiz it means the exponent rule x<sup>a</sup>/x<sup>b</sup> = x<sup>a−b</sup>."
    }
  ],
